{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/66598-what-are-you-planning-for-wtf","id":66598,"title":"What are you planning for WtF?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-06T11:24:11-08:00","id":66598,"title":"What are you planning for WtF?","content":"Right now I'm running a VtR:Blood and Smoke game, but I'm terribly excited about the Idigam Chronicle, so I've already started planning a werewolf &quot;sequel&quot; to my VtR game, which is set in Seattle 1982.<br /> <br /> Assuming that &quot;Furry, rage monster spirit cops&quot; is still the focus of Idigam Chronicle, the idea I've got so far is that what the players were doing in Seattle will cause ripples in the neighboring wilderness of Washington and British Columbia and start coming to a head in the early 1990s. Cue the PC wolves.<br /> <br /> How exactly the spiritual trouble will manifest I haven't decided yet, since I'm still getting into NWoD, but I'm looking forward to it nonetheless.<br /> <br /> What are y'all planning in regards to future Werewolf games, using Idigam Chronicles or otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T11:37:40-08:00","id":66610,"title":"","content":"A werewolf game set in Baghdad in 2013. Politics, religious strife, crime, elder horrors and a seriously messed up Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T11:40:49-08:00","id":66615,"title":"","content":"If I continue to play Werewolf I'm thinking that the pack may get reinforcement by a Pure defector, which will lead to all manner of strange situations. The idea is that the war between the Forsaken and the Pure in this region will cause all manner of stuff to bleed over on the pack's territory until the pack finally comes to actually confronting a pack of the Pure. On the list is also...<br /> <br /> * More havoc caused by local spirits<br /> <br /> * An Magoth coming into town from the countryside where it starts to cause nastiness<br /> <br /> * A group of Wolf-blooded Uratha hunters, and since they are kin to the local Forsaken is that outright massacre is not an option<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T12:49:02-08:00","id":66662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/66598-what-are-you-planning-for-wtf?p=66610#post66610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf game set in Baghdad in 2013. Politics, religious strife, crime, elder horrors and a seriously messed up Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, I wouldn't want to be a werewolf then and there. Messed up Shadow is right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:58:40-08:00","id":66761,"title":"","content":"The Idigam Chronicles isn't even likely to come out for two months. And I just checked and it's been pushed back to more than that.<br /> <br /> But that hasn't stopped me from starting to think about it since December. Because I'm a goon, a goon who loves Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my Changeling game is over, and while I'm running Blood and Smoke (the players and I enjoying the new system) it looks like I get to be a player again when Idigam Chronicles comes out, woo.<br /> <br /> Obviously everything could change when the game comes out, but I'll likely be playing a Mental character (my first character was Physical, and my last one was Social, I had a Mental character in between but the game didn't last long) and I've been encouraged by the ST to be a bad guy. So when the book comes out we'll see if that means a darker-themed shaman (huge fan of the Spirit, didn't get as involved in it as I wanted to the first time) or perhaps some other option will be available.<br /> <br /> Just from what I know of the ST, there'll likely be some repercussions from previous games. I know in our Changeling game we ran across a werewolf that had been severely traumatized by the actions of our werewolves in a previous game, so probably some more things like that. But no idea where the setting will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T19:57:42-08:00","id":66933,"title":"","content":"Well, I have a game right now that is about rebuilding the city from the events that happened in the previous game. Bale Hounds infiltrated most packs of the city and instigated a total war of Forsaken versus Pure, with the help of an Idigam that was found trapped in Joelma, a building that caught fire decades ago, and is now a major wound. The game ended with the death of the Idigam, but most packs dead, and the ones left alive don't trust each other anymore (fear of Bale Hound infiltration). Lot's of unprotected locus, major Bale Hound infestation in the city, a very nasty place to have a territory. Now seems like the players plan on uniting the packs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When Dark Eras come out, I'm planing a mini-chronicle set in 70s Sao Paulo (Which will probably have a lot in common with NYC in the 70s ;D). Players pack will run the Joelma territory. And one day, an Idigam will arrive and they will hunt it into the building.<br /> <br /> I also plan on doing a Viking one-shot one day. Might be cool as hell. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T20:12:44-08:00","id":66941,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping to wrap up Detroit Rock City before Idigam comes out. I have a lot of ideas for my next game but haven't decided yet if it'll be Forsaken or not. I've been considering Vampire, a Zombie Apocalypse game using NWoD rules and even an updated Demon: The Fallen. Who knows, though - I might run another Forsaken campaign, though nowhere near as long as Detroit Rock City.<br /> <br /> I'll definitely be recruiting here and on RPG.net for new players when the time comes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","name":"Mr. Shopping","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:25:21-08:00","id":67151,"title":"","content":"I'm planning on running a Ancient Sumerian werewolf game. Because werewolves + Sumer = awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:40:59-08:00","id":67161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/66598-what-are-you-planning-for-wtf?p=67151#post67151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm planning on running a Ancient Sumerian werewolf game. Because werewolves + Sumer = awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate more on that? I know that Sumer was mentioned a few times in the Forsaken core book, but it's been a while since I read that and I didn't get any of the supplements since it was such a non-starter with my local group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:58:38-08:00","id":67165,"title":"","content":"Back in Sumer, the Uratha were not yet Forsaken by the Spirit world. They where <i>Ur-Sag</i>, wolf-kings, and they lorded over man and spirit; walking amongst the world clothed in Gauru in all their terrifying glory as half-gods. They built a city in which the Ziggurat <i>Teppe Magath</i> sat proclaiming all their glory in both flesh and spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:14:48-08:00","id":67175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/66598-what-are-you-planning-for-wtf?p=67165#post67165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in Sumer, the Uratha were not yet Forsaken by the Spirit world</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. There were still Forsaken and Pure, the split had happened, spirits still plotted against the Forsaken, but they were accepted by mankind and can roam around in gauru form freely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T07:17:06-08:00","id":67176,"title":"","content":"Well, the spirits served them, but they didn't like it. So, not quite forsaken. There is a split, and I explained it in my game as such; <br /> <br /> <i>It was then that Iduth-Nanna bade us to protect nascent humanity. We were to shepherd them from their prideful state, and keep them from ravaging the world. We were forbid to hunt them for their flesh any longer. So, the eight children and the tribes of Ur-Farah convened. This new commandment was debated, for six days, and seven nights. On the morning of the seventh day a vote was held. Five of the eight voted that them and their tribe would uphold the commandment of Iduth-Nanna, the other three grew angry. They said that humanity would harm the mother Akihana. They named themselves the Pure and left, vowing to be enemies of humanity and their protectors, the Ur-Sag.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T09:48:47-08:00","id":67251,"title":"","content":"I just started a campaign of Storm Lords who have appointed themselves to the task of traveling the country and &quot;teaching&quot; other packs how to &quot;fix&quot; their territory. They also seem to gravitate to pack-less territories that need help. When the new chronicle hits I plan on adding it to the list of problems they face from one town to the next. I hope to be able to slowly revel to them whatever new troubles will come from the book and build some suspense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T11:51:41-08:00","id":67309,"title":"","content":"My group tends to skip between games once per story/adventure. Right now we are playing our W:tF game, set in the Yukon were unlike many normal W:tF the pack holds a large territory because there are so few in that region of the world. They have to rely on each other as there is little outside help. Currently they are dealing with a particularly nasty spirit who is disrupting their small town, and getting their first taste of the Beshilu while being hinted toward the true threat of the chronicle, a Maeljin that is moving south from the north pole, that every pack in the Yukon will have to contend with.<br /> <br /> Next up is a Savage Worlds story which I already have prepared but after that we switch to V:tR for the first time since Blood &amp; Smoke hit and I can't wait to make the switch. Hopefully by the time our W:tF game roles around (3-5 months) Idigam Chronicle will be out or at least large parts revealed to the fans that I can start switching over. For now Look's (Pendragon's) house rules and revamped gifts have helped make our W:tF game fantastic so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T14:59:22-08:00","id":68088,"title":"","content":"My plans are finishing the 100+ page overhaul and revision I've been working on with a friend/Co-ST the last few months (soon!); Idigam Chronicles isn't on the roster yet without any hard info on what's being looked at done; too hush hush and I've still got a few months of games to run for my players. Hell, it may not even fit our ongoing game at all, whereas what's been worked on specifically addresses what we and our players wanted to see. My plans are to get all the Werewolf players on what we've got rolling, play with it, refine it, see what Idigam Chronicles brings for material we want to use, and go from there.<br /> <br /> Once the overhaul doc is done I'll share the link or PDF with you lot to play around with and see what you think; it has a few smaller areas to address, though though overall mechanical meat and some revised explanations of core ideas are done (fiction and similar suggestions will be for later if it turns into a popular fan project or something else).<br /> <br /> Can't please everyone, obviously, but we're already working on converting our players over, and so far they're stoked. The Instincts (now tweaked slightly more) are only the tip of the iceberg. Might fit the tastes of some forumites quite a bit better than what has been bandied about, likely won't be the tastes of some, but there is likely material to be used from it that folks will like regardless of how much is used. Fair warning, it's not going to be the finalized version; we have to play around with it more to see how things roll with our crew, so I'm assuming there will be ongoing tweaks and possibly some eventual incorporation of Idigam Chronicles material some months down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}